{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS issue. To get started, I need to identify your account. Could you please provide your phone number, customer ID, or your full name and date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, I’ll need to check a few things on your phone. First, can you try sending a picture message (MMS) using your default messaging app and let me know if it still fails? This will help confirm the issue is ongoing."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming. Next, let's check if your phone currently has cellular service, as MMS requires a network connection. Please look at your phone's status bar and let me know if you see any signal bars or if it says 'No Service' or shows the airplane mode icon."
}

{
  "message": "The airplane mode icon means your phone is not connected to any network, which will prevent MMS from working. Please turn off airplane mode on your phone. Once it’s off, check your status bar again to see if you have signal bars. Let me know if you see signal bars or if the issue persists."
}

{
  "message": "Great, your phone now has network service and data enabled. Please try sending a picture message (MMS) again using your default messaging app. Let me know if it goes through or if you still experience the same issue."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. Since you have service and data enabled, let's check if your mobile data connection is working properly, as MMS requires mobile data. Please run a speed test on your phone and let me know if it completes successfully or if it says 'no connection.'"
}

{
  "message": "Since your speed test says 'No Connection,' your mobile data is currently unavailable. Let's check if you are traveling outside your usual service area. Are you currently traveling or in a different location than usual? This will help determine if data roaming settings might be affecting your connection."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, being abroad can affect your ability to use mobile data and send MMS if data roaming is not enabled. Please check your phone’s settings and let me know if data roaming is currently turned on. If it is off, please turn it on and try running the speed test again. Let me know the result."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking your settings. I have now enabled international roaming on your line, which is required for mobile data and MMS to work while you are abroad. Please try running the speed test again, and then try sending a picture message. Let me know if your connection and MMS are now working."
}

{
  "message": "Since you now have roaming enabled and data roaming is turned on, but you still have no mobile data connection, we should check your mobile data settings. Please check if mobile data is turned on in your phone’s settings. If it is off, turn it on and try the speed test again. If it is already on and you still have no connection, let me know."
}

{
  "message": "It looks like you have used 15.1GB of data, which is over your plan's monthly data limit of 15GB. This is likely why your mobile data and MMS are not working. Would you like to add more data (up to 2GB) to your plan for this month, or are you interested in changing to a plan with a higher data limit? Please let me know how you’d like to proceed."
}

{
  "message": "How much extra data would you like to add? You can refuel up to 2GB. Please let me know if you want to add 1GB or 2GB, and I’ll confirm the price before proceeding."
}

{
  "message": "The price to add 2GB of extra data to your plan is $4.00 (at $2.00 per GB). Would you like to proceed with this purchase and add 2GB of data to your line?"
}

{
  "message": "2GB of extra data has been successfully added to your line for $4.00. Please try running the speed test again and then send a picture message to check if your MMS is now working. Let me know if you need any further assistance."
}

{
  "message": "Since your mobile data connection is now excellent but MMS still isn't working, let's check your network technology. Please check your phone's network mode and let me know if it is set to 2G, 3G, 4G, or 5G. MMS requires at least 3G or higher. If it's set to 2G only, please change it to include 3G, 4G, or 5G and try sending an MMS again."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming your network mode. Next, let's check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled, as it can sometimes interfere with MMS. Please check your phone's settings and let me know if Wi-Fi Calling is turned on. If it is, please turn it off and then try sending an MMS again."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking. Next, let's make sure your default messaging app has the necessary permissions. Please check your app settings and confirm that the messaging app has both storage and SMS permissions enabled. If either permission is missing, please enable it and try sending an MMS again. Let me know the result."
}

{
  "message": "To enable the required permissions, please go to your phone's settings, find the default messaging app, and grant both storage and SMS permissions. Once you have enabled these permissions, try sending an MMS message again and let me know if it works."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear your MMS is working now! If you have any other questions or need assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS issue. First, I need to identify your account to assist you further. Could you please provide your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, could you please try sending a picture message (MMS) using your default messaging app and let me know if it works or if you receive any error message? This will help me confirm the current status before we proceed with troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming. Let's start by checking if your phone currently has cellular service, as MMS requires a network connection. Could you please check your phone's status bar and let me know if you see any signal bars or if it says 'No Service' or shows the airplane mode icon?"
}

{
  "message": "Please turn off Airplane Mode on your phone. Once you have done that, check your status bar again to see if you have signal bars and if the airplane mode icon disappears. Let me know if your service is restored or if you still have issues."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the update. Next, let's check your SIM card status to ensure it's being recognized by your phone. Please check your phone's SIM status and let me know if it shows as active, missing, or locked with a PIN/PUK code."
}

{
  "message": "Please try removing your SIM card from your phone and then carefully re-inserting it. After you have done this, check your phone's SIM status again to see if it is now detected and active. Let me know if your service is restored or if you still see the same issue."
}

{
  "message": "Your SIM card is now detected, which is good progress. Since you have a weak signal and are connected to 2G, let's try to improve your connection and enable data. Please check your phone's network mode preference and let me know if it is set to 2G only, or if 3G/4G/5G options are available. Also, check if mobile data is enabled on your device."
}

{
  "message": "Please change your network mode preference to include 3G, 4G, or 5G if available. After that, enable mobile data on your device. Once both changes are made, try sending an MMS message again and let me know if it works or if you encounter any issues."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for updating those settings. Next, let's check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled on your device, as it can sometimes interfere with MMS. Please check your Wi-Fi Calling status and let me know if it is ON or OFF."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please turn off Wi-Fi Calling and then try sending an MMS message again using your default messaging app. Let me know if this resolves the issue or if you are still unable to send MMS messages."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for trying that. Next, let's check if your default messaging app has the necessary permissions. Please check the app permissions for your messaging app and confirm that it has both storage and SMS permissions enabled. Let me know if either of these permissions is missing, or if both are already granted."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please grant storage permission to your messaging app. After granting the permission, try sending an MMS message again. Let me know if this resolves the issue or if you are still unable to send MMS messages."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for updating the permissions. The next step is to check your phone's APN (Access Point Name) settings, as incorrect APN settings can prevent MMS from working. Please check your APN settings and let me know if there is an MMSC URL configured. If you do not see an MMSC URL, please let me know."
}

{
  "message": "Please reset your APN settings to the carrier defaults. After resetting, try sending an MMS message again using your default messaging app. Let me know if this resolves the issue or if you are still unable to send MMS messages."
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}
